<?xml version="1.0"?>
<!--
  robot: XLeRobot | consumers: controller_manager, robot_state_publisher, RViz, CAD Viewer
  units: metres, kilograms, seconds, radians | frames: +X forward, +Y left, +Z up
  source: Vector-Wangel/XLeRobot b017b5e6354bd9f61f4247a920c72622ca0aade0 simulation/mujoco/xlerobot.xml
  root: base_footprint (frame-only); base_link is the upstream chassis, 0.035 m above ground.
  Odom starts with base heading zero; upstream initial world yaw of pi/2 is removed in the bridge.
  Each physical link corresponds to its identically named MJCF body except chassis becomes base_link.
  Joint frames use the MJCF body orientation and the joint's local anchor; visual/COM offsets compensate.
  Joint axes, zero poses, and limits are copied from compiled MJCF; positive signs match upstream qpos.
  Mesh filenames/scales and visual poses are from raw MJCF and pinned ManiSkill URDF, before mesh recentering.
  meshes: meshes/ contains MuJoCo assets; full_meshes/ contains ManiSkill cart, mounts, head and wrist cameras.
  Grippers: full ManiSkill Fixed_Jaw.stl, Fixed_Jaw_Motor.stl and Moving_Jaw.stl; *_part meshes are collision hulls only.
  Gripper visual origins remain identity, copied from the upstream visual declarations.
  Additional visuals copy the pinned ManiSkill URDF transforms/scales with the common cart Z correction; arm mounts and shoulder zero poses use the full ManiSkill assembly beside the tower.
  Head support and pan/tilt zero frames now match the complete upstream ManiSkill head assembly.
  Visual-only fixed bodies including cart connectors omit inertia and collision; the transparent cart mass/collision proxy is hidden.
  Explicit per-mesh scales preserve mixed source units.
  Cart body visual: owned white finish (0.95,0.95,0.95,1); original caster colors retained.
  inertials: original compiled values except base_link: assumed 8 kg cart box, dimensions 0.4 x 0.4 x 0.76 m.
  Cart assembly Z correction -0.0359257260090011 m aligns caster tyre bottoms with omniwheel contact plane.
  Cart COM Z shifted by the same correction; box inertia computed as m*(b^2+c^2)/12.
  Four passive swivel/rolling casters are internal MuJoCo joints; ROS caster visuals show their zero pose.
  Caster tyre/mount compliance: passive +/-2 mm vertical travel, 15000 N/m spring, 30 Ns/m damping (simulation estimates).
  Their 0.1 kg forks and 0.15 kg wheels are allocated from the 8 kg cart estimate, preserving aggregate inertia.
  Three fixed cart_connector_N links use the upstream printed connector STL, scaled in Z to the mesh-derived gap.
  Connector XY uses drive motor mount centers as a simulation fit; hardware bolt positions are unverified.
  tools/prepare_cart_mount.py records the geometry calculation and mesh partition; cart_mount.yaml stores results.
  MuJoCo has a free chassis and 48 passive omni rollers adapted from Aditya Kamath lekiwi_mujoco.
  Roller masses/inertias are allocated from the source wheel mass, preserving aggregate wheel inertia.
  Passive roller joints are internal physics geometry, omitted from ROS control/visualization.
  Nominal base height is 0.035 m; wheel contacts allow vertical, pitch and roll movement.
  Wheel radius 0.0508 m (4-inch CAD wheel); mean wheel-center radius 0.12851666666666667 m; offset pi.
  Other imported link inertias remain estimates from upstream, not measured hardware data.
  No URDF collisions: dynamics/contact geometry remain owned by MJCF, this description is for ROS visualization.
  Camera: head_tilt_link -> head_camera_link at (0.055,0,0.0225), from upstream ManiSkill URDF.
  RGB optical center: (0,0.02,0) in camera link, REP-103 optical rotation (-pi/2,0,-pi/2).
  Assumption: aligned depth and RGB share this optical center in simulation; no stereo baseline is simulated.
  Camera housing: existing upstream tophead5/tophead6 meshes on head_tilt_link; no added box or mass.
  Assumption: imu_link is a 0.02 m cube of mass 0.005 kg at (0,0,-0.015) in base_link,
  under the printed base plate; orientation matches base_link. Exact hardware mount is provisional.
  Head servo effort/velocity are simulation allowances, not hardware specifications.
  Control: velocity interfaces for three wheel servos; position interfaces for arms/head.
  SimulatorSystem uses joint state/command shared memory with one MuJoCo physics owner.
  Contact-driven base: commanded wheel joints plus internal passive rollers/casters; no planar chassis actuation.
  Wheel command cap +/-20 rad/s is a simulation allowance; hardware calibration is separate.
  Frame-only links: base_footprint, head_camera_link, head_camera_rgb_optical_frame.
-->
